# SAEA-E-002 "R4 context-dose" on the FAST iteration split.
#
# Same three arms and the same experiment fragment as
# docs/arms/r4-context-dose.arms, but on `fast-e21-sub3` (the three shortest of
# the frozen ten): 122 slices instead of 614, about 21 minutes per arm instead
# of 2.5 hours.
#
# **The fast split is biased by construction** — shortest-first, not seeded, so
# it over-represents short calls. Everything run here is directional. The
# monotonicity result this experiment exists to establish (mismatched ≥
# nocontext ≥ matched) is re-run on `r4-e21-sub10` before it is claimed, and at
# n=3 the exact-Wilcoxon two-sided p floor is 2/2**3 = 0.25, so per-sample
# significance is unreachable here by construction — read corpus WER and the
# direction of the per-sample deltas, nothing else.
#
# run_id:baseline_fragment
SAEA-E-002F-r4-nocontext:bare-core-ojw
SAEA-E-002F-r4-matched:fixed-legal-context-ojw
SAEA-E-002F-r4-mismatched:mismatched-evidence-ojw
